# Cadence architecture

Cadence is a Next.js 14 (App Router) AI-powered calendar/task app, plus a
separate Chrome extension build in `extension/`. The AI agent learns actual
task durations and auto-distributes tasks across free calendar slots.

## Layers

- `app/api/**/route.ts` — API routes: assignments (AI decompose), auth
  (Google OAuth), calendar (events/feed/push/sync), google calendars,
  ics proxy, learning (calibration/profile), telemetry.
- `app/**/page.tsx`, `app/layout.tsx` — Next.js pages/routes.
- `components/*.tsx` — UI: `Calendar`, `TaskManager`, `AIAgentPanel`,
  `NotificationsBell`, `LegalPageShell`, `ReadableDescription`,
  `AppProviders`.
- `lib/*.ts` — business logic (Google Calendar integration, ICS
  parsing/export, calendar feed sync/store, AI agent, learning/estimate
  calibration, storage, date/time/schedule utils).
- `lib/i18n/*` — i18n context + en/ko message catalogs.
- `extension/src/*` — standalone Chrome extension (panel, background,
  content script, options) — mostly independent of `app/`.
- `types/index.ts` — shared type definitions (`Task`, `CalendarEvent`, etc.),
  imported almost everywhere.
- `tests/*` — Vitest tests, largely mirror `lib/`.

## Most depended-on modules (highest fan-in — read these first)

1. `types/index.ts` (20 importers) — shared `Task`/`CalendarEvent`/etc. types.
2. `lib/decompose-assignment.ts` (10) — AI breakdown of an assignment into
   subtasks/steps.
3. `lib/calendar-feed-events.ts` (8) — calendar feed event generation.
4. `lib/estimate-calibration.ts` (7) — learns/calibrates duration estimates.
5. `lib/date-utils.ts` (7) — date helpers used across lib/components.
6. `lib/schedule-constants.ts` (6) — work-hours/scheduling constants.
7. `lib/google-calendar.ts` (5) — Google Calendar client logic.
8. `lib/storage.ts` (5) — localStorage persistence.
9. `lib/google-calendar-rest.ts` (4) — raw Google Calendar REST calls.
10. `lib/ai-agent.ts` (4) — auto-schedules tasks into free calendar slots.

## Conventions

- Path alias `@/*` maps to the repo root (see `tsconfig.json`).
- API routes are thin; scheduling/AI/calibration logic lives in `lib/`.
- `extension/` has its own esbuild config and does not share Next.js
  build tooling with `app/`.

